  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.7,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U4", "U6", "U3"],
      "pins": ["U4.1", "U4.2", "U6.6", "U3.13"],
      "nets": ["NET0001", "NET0002"],
      "observed": "On the MCU sheet the heater high-side switch U4 (TPS1H200AQDGNRQ1) has pin 1 (IN) on net NET0002 and pin 2 (DIAG_EN) on a different net NET0001. NET0002 is the ESP32 GPIO1/HEATER net (U3 pin 13) and the heater status-LED path (J6/D8/R6). NET0001 is, however, also the chip-select net of thermocouple U6 (MAX31855KASA pin 6, Thermocouples sheet). So the heater switch's DIAG_EN is merged onto a thermocouple SPI chip-select line instead of being tied to IN/GPIO1.",
      "expected": "The specification states the heater switch is 'driven by ESP32 GPIO1 on both IN and DIAG_EN' and 'IN/DIAG_EN (pins 1/2) are both driven from ESP32 GPIO1 (net /Microcontroller/HEATER)'. Pins 1 and 2 must share the HEATER/GPIO1 net, and each thermocouple CS net must connect only to its own MAX31855 CS pin and its MCU GPIO, not to the heater switch.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "MCU sheet (page 3): U4 TPS1H200AQDGNRQ1 — 'DIAG_EN 2' carries label NET0001, 'IN 1' carries label NET0002; U3 GPIO1/ADC1_CH1/XTAL_32K_N (pin 13) carries label NET0002"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Thermocouples sheet (page 5): U6 MAX31855KASA — 'CS 6' carries label NET0001"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "driven by ESP32 GPIO1 on both IN and DIAG_EN ... IN/DIAG_EN (pins 1/2) are both driven from ESP32 GPIO1 (net /Microcontroller/HEATER)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The smart high-side switch's diagnostic-enable input is driven by a thermocouple chip-select line rather than held with the heater drive. During sequential thermocouple polling, DIAG_EN toggles with U6's CS, so the TPS1H200's diagnostic/FAULT reporting is coupled to thermocouple selection instead of to the heater control signal — a deviation from the intended wiring that changes the heater switch's fault-reporting behaviour.",
      "confidence": 0.7
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic matches the specification on power rails, the power mux, the buck regulator, the thermocouple SPI topology (shared SCK/SO, three independent CS) and the heater switch's VS/CL/FAULT/OUT/GND pins, but the heater switch's DIAG_EN (U4 pin 2) is wired onto a thermocouple chip-select net (NET0001, shared with U6 pin 6) instead of being tied to the IN/HEATER net (NET0002) as the spec requires — a bridged-nets anomaly."
}

